From c1f127b3cbf88a2945a97d42f681b46d73bec61d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:09:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): browser build saves, posts as downloads and greys
 the file commands it cannot run

In the wasm build every file dialog answered "cancelled" and only logged
it, so Open, Save, Save As and Post did nothing on screen.

- app: project::save_text and posting::post_setup_unwritten return the
  bytes the desktop writes (same collect, gate and engine run); save and
  post_setup now call them, so the two cannot drift.
- ui: browser_files hands the bytes to the browser as a download (Blob,
  object URL, anchor click through eframe::web_sys; Save As asks the name
  with window.prompt). Save, Save As, the unsaved prompt's Save and Post
  download in the browser.
- ui: browser_files::refusal names every command the browser cannot run
  yet (open pickers, recent files, folders, the four exports); State::run
  refuses them on the status line, ribbon cells and page buttons are
  greyed with the reason as their tip.

Open paths stay owed to PR #1314; the exports to #1437.

Refs #1431

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
